[step] Wrong planar-step classification of the relaxed wing's continuous cubic extrusion. The reported parallel planes are fitted to adjacent bands of its tessellation. Each hook side is one extruded Bezier edge in _fixed_pump_mount._wing; the native/source identity review confirms the exported smooth shape. There is no 0.040 mm step or added cutout in the native hook. The relaxed and seated tip poses are geometrical states, not a computed elastic response.
alternatives: A straight hook face would change the approved smooth relaxed-to-seated wing pose. Adding or trimming a 0.040 mm ledge would create the defect the classifier incorrectly reports.
